    "vegetationWeatheringComment": [
      "Weathering for everything that grows. Same three terms as every other",
      "boundary in this game (see environment.weathering), aimed at the two",
      "boundaries a plant has: where it meets the ground, and where it meets",
      "the air.",
      "  noiseTileWorldSize - how far apart the fields' features land. Small,",
      "    because a plant is small; the ore edge reads the same tile at",
      "    thousands of world units.",
      "  barkTileWorldSize / foliageTileWorldSize / grassTileWorldSize - the",
      "    WORLD size of one wrap of each surface's own tile. These replace",
      "    uv-space repeats: sampled through uvs, a big tree and a small tree",
      "    wore bark at different physical sizes, which is the texel-density",
      "    rule broken on the most numerous object in the world. Sampling by",
      "    world position also makes every instance unique for free, which is",
      "    legal here only because props never move.",
      "  baseGrimeHeightWorldUnits - how far up from a plant's own base the",
      "    soil reaches. A trunk meeting the ground in a clean line is the",
      "    same tell as an ore edge meeting the ground in a clean line.",
      "  dry* - the dissolve. Patches of a canopy are dead and patches of a",
      "    sward are straw, and which is which is decided per patch by the",
      "    grain rather than spread evenly, so the crown stops reading as one",
      "    solid faceted mass.",
      "  dust* - what settles on upward-facing surfaces. Gated on the normal's",
      "    up component, so the tops of leaves pale and their undersides do",
      "    not - which is most of what separates a canopy from a green shape."
    ],
    "vegetationWeathering": {
