    "weatheringComment": [
      "The shared weathering vocabulary. Every treatment that dirties a",
      "boundary in this game - the ore region edge, the plateau wall rims, the",
      "vegetation - reads THIS noise tile, at its own world scale. A second",
      "noise tile would be a second vocabulary, and two treatments that meet",
      "on screen would stop looking like the same weather.",
      "  resolution - texels per axis of the tile. It carries three",
      "    independent scalar fields in R/G/B (mottle, grain, blotch); alpha",
      "    is not a fourth, because a Canvas 2D surface premultiplies and a",
      "    field stored in alpha would scale the three stored in RGB.",
      "How far apart the fields' features land in the world is each host's",
      "own noiseTileWorldSize, because a tree and a plateau weather at",
      "different scales even though they weather by the same mechanism."
    ],
    "weathering": {
