      },
      "soilTextureComment": [
        "The ONE substance every weathered boundary is buried under - the ore",
        "region's dirty rim, the debris at the bottom of a plateau wall, the",
        "spall along its top, the dirt at the base of a tree. Dust and grit is",
        "dust and grit; hosts differ only in the tint and exposure they read it",
        "through, never in which tile they read. tileWorldSize is shared for",
        "the same reason texel density is: a dry pale wall rim and a damp dark",
        "tree base have to be the same physical grain or they stop reading as",
        "one weather."
      ],
