        "resolution": 4096,
        "blend": 0.3,
        "litColorBlend": 0.55,
        "contrast": 0.9,
        "roughnessVariation": 0.1,
        "tileWorldSize": 2000,
        "fineComment": "The same rock tile read again small, rotated and co-prime to the plate-scale read - the grit between the plates, exactly as world.terrain.rock reads its own fine octave. At one octave the ore was the one smooth surface on the map. Same sampler; the terrain program is at the 16-unit ceiling.",
        "fineTileWorldSize": 560,
        "fineBlend": 0.4
      },
      "standardMaterial": {
        "metalness": 0.5,
        "roughness": 0.88
      },
      "edgeComment": [
        "How the ore region MEETS the ground. Without this the region field's",
        "own contour is drawn straight, which reads as a clean stencilled",
        "silhouette - correct, and obviously authored. Real ore weathers out",
        "into the soil around it, so the boundary is displaced, dissolved, and",
        "buried under a band of dirt whose thickness varies along its length.",
        "  growWorldUnits    - the contour is pushed OUTWARD by this much before",
        "                      it is warped, so the erosion below eats back into",
        "                      spare ore instead of shrinking a small deposit.",
        "  warpWorldUnits    - peak displacement of the contour, in world units.",
        "                      This moves where ore is DRAWN, never where it is",
        "                      mined: the authoritative cells are untouched.",
        "  blendBand*        - half-width of the ore-to-ground ramp. Random per",
        "                      location between the two, which is what makes the",
        "                      transition read as varying in thickness.",
        "  grainStrength     - 0 takes the ramp straight (a clean soft edge); 1",
        "                      dissolves it against the granular field, so inside",
        "                      the band the ore is either present or absent and",
        "                      the grain decides which. Minification averages the",
        "                      grain back to its mean, so a zoomed-out edge",
        "                      recovers the smooth ramp instead of aliasing.",
        "  grime*Reach       - how far the dirt band reaches in from the ore side",
        "                      and out onto the ground side, before variation.",
        "                      Deliberately unequal: dirt SPILLS off the ore onto",
        "                      the ground; two near-equal reaches trace the contour.",
        "  grimeThicknessVariation - +/- fraction those reaches are jittered by,",
        "                      at two scales along the rim (SurfaceWeathering3D",
        "                      WEATHER_FIELD_TAPS reach / reachFine), so no two",
        "                      stretches of one rim share a width.",
        "  grimeFalloff      - >1 concentrates the dirt at the contour itself.",
        "                      The MEAN profile: it swings 0.6x-1.6x along the",
        "                      rim, and the band's far edge is dissolved against",
        "                      the grain rather than faded (weatherGrimeBand).",
        "  grimePatchDepth   - how much the grit field can thin the band, so the",
        "                      dirt is patchy rather than an even halo.",
        "  grimeStrength     - how much of the dirt texture replaces the surface.",
        "  grimeDarken       - multiplier applied at full grime; this is the dark",
        "                      seam where metal meets land.",
        "  grimeSeamPower    - exponent the DARKENING alone takes. High values",
        "                      pin the dark line tight against the contour and",
        "                      leave the rest of the band at the dirt colour -",
        "                      which, once the metal reflection is matted away,",
        "                      renders LIGHTER than the metal interior, and",
        "                      grime that lightens what it covers reads wrong.",
        "                      Authored near 1 so the darkening rides the whole",
        "                      band: dirt over metal must always land darker",
        "                      than the metal it buries.",
        "  grimeMatte        - how much of the ore's metalness/reflection the",
        "                      dirt suppresses. Dirt is not shiny, and a rim that",
        "                      keeps its specular still reads as a clean edge",
        "                      however dark it is painted.",
        "TRAP: growWorldUnits + warpWorldUnits + the largest jittered reach must",
        "stay inside metalDepositConfig.surfaceField.edgeRangeWorldUnits. Past",
        "that the field saturates, so the distance stops varying and the band",
        "would terminate in a hard ring. Pinned by contract test."
      ],
      "edge": {
